  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-session-fork",
      "text": "English | [简体中文](docs/README.zh.md)\n\nSub agents and parallel development never quite deliver in today's agent apps. This project manages dsh's native, discrete sessions the way git manages branches: `fork` gives conversations inheritance, while `squash` and `rebase` give them merging — a major upgrade to the parallel-development and prompt-management experience on dsh.\n\nThis is a plugin for `DeepSeek Harness`; it cannot run standalone."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-session-fork",
      "text": "Version `0.4.0` supports dsh `0.2.1-rc.2`. It replaces the previous dsh `0.1.2-rc.1` compatibility line; upgrade dsh before upgrading this plugin.\n\nFor compatibility development, build a sibling `../deepseek-harness` checkout and run `bun run test:harness`. Set `DSH_HARNESS_DIR` to use another checkout. The check uses an isolated copy linked to the actual harness packages and checks V4 messages, historical merges, and both Host and Client types."
    },
    {
      "section": "Pain points it solves",
      "text": "- **Efficient solo parallel development**: the branch model mirrors how real programmers collaborate. While developing in parallel, every agent holds its own snapshot of the repo — you trade a strictly linear development history for resolving conflicts at merge time.\n- **Clean context management**: the main branch (e.g. `main`) stays your secretary and dispatcher. Research and coding tasks are delegated to child branches; when a task is done, only its compressed context is reported back to the main branch.\n- **Hardened session management**: the branch model upgrades dsh's native `fork` and cross-session messaging experience."
    },
    {
